  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <h3>How do I open ShakeFree Mouse?</h3>
  <p>It lives in the tray by the clock: a round blue icon with a white pointer (grey when ShakeFree Mouse is off). Click the <strong>^</strong> arrow if you can’t see it. Double-click the icon to open the settings.</p>

  <h3>How do I turn ShakeFree Mouse on or off?</h3>
  <p>Use the big <strong>ShakeFree Mouse is on / off</strong> switch at the top of the settings, right-click the tray icon and choose <strong>Turned on</strong>, or press <strong>Ctrl+Shift+F9</strong> from anywhere. When it’s off, your mouse works as if the app wasn’t there. Smoothing also has its own switch further down, which is on by default.</p>

  <h3>What is Super-smoothing?</h3>
  <p>An extra-slow mode for small buttons and links: the pointer glides towards your hand even more slowly, so you can choose the moment it lands. Turn it on and off with the key below Esc (<strong>§</strong> on Nordic keyboards, <strong>`</strong> on US ones), or with <strong>Super-smoothing on</strong> in the tray menu. While ShakeFree Mouse and smoothing are on, that key switches Super-smoothing instead of typing. You can set its strength, and choose another key, in the settings.</p>

  <h3>Why does the pointer glide behind my hand?</h3>
  <p>That’s the smoothing at work. The higher the <strong>Smoothing strength</strong>, the more shaking it removes, and the more slowly the pointer follows your hand. If it feels too slow, lower the strength a step or two.</p>

  <h3>Does it work with a touchpad or a pen?</h3>
  <p>Yes. ShakeFree Mouse smooths a mouse, a trackball, a touchpad or a pen.</p>

  <h3>How does the free trial work?</h3>
  <p>You get 5 days with everything included, from the first time you start the app. No card is needed. When the trial ends, ShakeFree Mouse pauses and your mouse works as normal until you enter a key.</p>

  <h3>I bought a key. How do I activate it?</h3>
  <p>Click <strong>Activate</strong> on the confirmation page or in your receipt email. Or open ShakeFree Mouse, click <strong>Enter key</strong>, then <strong>Paste</strong> (a copied key fills in by itself) and <strong>Activate</strong>.</p>

  <h3>Can I use my key on another PC?</h3>
  <p>Yes, each key works on up to 3 PCs. To move it, open the settings on the old PC and choose <strong>Remove from this PC</strong> under General, then activate it on the new one.</p>

  <h3>How do I change or cancel my plan?</h3>
  <p>Open the settings and click <strong>Manage plan</strong> under General, or use the link in your receipt email from Lemon Squeezy.</p>

  <h3>The pointer isn’t smoothed in some programs</h3>
  <p>Over windows that run as administrator, Windows may stop normal apps from steering the pointer, so it moves unsmoothed there. Games that read the mouse directly aren’t smoothed either. And while smoothing is on, Windows’ <strong>Enhance pointer precision</strong> isn’t used, so big, fast moves travel a little less far than you may be used to.</p>
